error: `open` holds the thread until it is done, and an async function does not hold its thread
  the tasks of async functions share a few threads: one that holds its thread keeps the others from running
  --> error_net_connect_blocking_call.sg:6:20
 6 |     var conn = try open("127.0.0.1:80")
   |                    ^^^^
  `open` does `TcpStream.connect` here:
  --> error_net_connect_blocking_call.sg:2:22
 2 |     return TcpStream.connect(address)
   |                      ^^^^^^^
  hint: a function that does it runs on a thread of its own with `await Task.run(work, x)`
